{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793706852,"nonce":"CFZy+sS/eVfYjH+yjgioBu2b5cM=","message":"Desktop editor attachment is committed in 486494a4ad002664a1fb6630c097b27367d18d16, with recovery/process and GC-wait guards in a8788694935a937563feccd7ef9988dacac43f1d. The rebuilt shared editor bundle is 463dc74fd3820bfa7c742236919de3c1d697f790.\n\nThe existing Haxe EditorDocuments adapter now also works over a native channel. Native workers reuse the session DocHub, provider, atomic private buffer format and accepted-head Save logic. A Git folder resolves its remembered workspace from the existing development gateway/account configuration. Native windows share a hub while retaining separate projections and author undo. Cloud requests coalesce during typing; the receiver sleeps without keeping a GC mutator active. Tab activation, edits and Save perform catch-up, without an idle network timer. A workspace/account-scoped OS lock prevents another process from overwriting the same private recovery, and releases on exit.\n\nLocal histories, unsaved recovery and Jam ownership are retained instead of reseeded. Unsupported and unbound files use their normal editor/Save path; fresh files also remain locally editable when the cloud cannot supply a graph. Save callbacks now use the accepted saved text, and rejected saves finish rather than leaving a pending UI operation.\n\nVerification: scripts/check-sync.sh passes the actual workbench snapshot/pull/conflict flow and the Haxe/native bridge against an independent browser client through the local Rust gateway. The final process check additionally refuses a competing process, restores private state after exit (including normalized gateway URLs), and explicitly collects garbage without a safepoint warning. The full native session regressions pass; the focused cloud/editor suite now has 12 passing cases covering late typing, save races, author undo, independent windows, Unicode, legacy passthrough and offline initial opens. Browser tests (79), Worker tests (42), and the shared Haxe editor checks pass. Native library, native app bytecode, release session and browser WASM have been rebuilt.\n\nThis issue remains open for explicit reconciliation/migration of existing local and browser histories. Production desktop account/sign-in integration remains separate from this development configuration. Pushed delivery is still 87a7cd157e91265a33566edeed409b32e26e47d3a1bcf8840a57e0d14907bcf6; cross-device continuous editor sync is not yet advertised. Deployed Cloudflare/MSB validation remains outstanding.","files":null}]}